  "chosen_label": "Mega Starmie ex (bench 2 · 330/330 · 1⚡)",
  "correct_label": "Cinderace (bench 1 · 30/130 · 1⚡)",
  "frame_key": "82756664|1|decision|97",
  "note": "82756664 f97 (TO_ACTIVE, mega_starmie seat 1, turn 9). Active KO'd; their Active is a Mega Lucario ex on 20/440 (Hero's Cape) — every benched body of mine Knocks it Out, and it is a Mega ex, so that Knock Out takes 3 prizes (5 -> 2). Bench: Cinderace 30/130 (1{W}), Mega Starmie ex 330/330 (1{W}), Staryu 70/70 (1{W}). Cinderace reads 130 max HP because it is a Stage 2 and their stadium is Gravity Mountain (-30 HP to each Stage 2); Mega Starmie ex is Stage 1 and untouched. Correct=[0] Cinderace.",
  "claims": {
    "decision": {
      "correct": [
        0
      ],
      "owner": "#165",
      "ruled": "2026-07-27",
      "why": "HELD OUT as a MANEUVER (ADR-0070 amendment J). The Knock Out is available to every candidate and yields the same 3 prizes, so it cancels; the decision is what else the promoted body does. Cinderace shields the 3-prize win-condition from the revenge attack AND its attack accelerates — and the user's winning line is a dependent step-chain the per-option equation structurally cannot price: Night Stretcher fetches the Mega Starmie ex from discard, evolve the Staryu, attach, Buddy-Buddy Poffin to thin, HARLEQUIN (their hand is 7 — the disruption), then Turbo Flare for the Knock Out, distributing its 3 Energy 1/2 so BOTH benched Mega Starmie ex end the turn on exactly 3 — the cost of Nebula Beam (●●● 210), so both are finishers rather than one stranded on Jetting Blow. The freshly evolved body starts on 1, not 0: evolution keeps attached cards (rules.md §4) and the Staryu already carried a {W}. Two defects sit behind it. (i) `_deck_basic_energy_fuel` returns 0 by the sound pigeonhole floor (9 Basic {W} in the decklist, 6 visible, 3 unseen against 5 face-down prizes -> max(0, 3-5) = 0), which zeroes the accel dividend; feeding it the 3 unseen copies instead flips the frame to correct decisively (Cinderace +175 vs the Mega -30). Filed separately: it is ADR-0061's oracle, pre-existing and shared with the attack option, not 1c's to change. (ii) Harlequin SHUFFLES THE HAND BACK INTO THE DECK before the attack, manufacturing the very fuel Turbo Flare then searches for — a property of the step ORDER that no decision-time deck read can see. That is #165's. ADR-0073 §4's exposure grading is EXONERATED: the counterfactual shows it was never the cause."
    }
  }
